{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Integrate MediaTailor SSAI with channel assembly for monetized linear channels","context":"## Defining ad breaks in channel assembly\n\nWhen creating programs in channel assembly, you can define ad breaks in several\nways:\n\nProgram transitions\n: Insert ads between programs in your channel schedule. This is the simplest\n approach and ensures ads don't interrupt program content.\n\nSCTE-35 markers\n: If your VOD content contains SCTE-35 markers, channel assembly can\n preserve these markers, and ad insertion can use them as ad break\n points.\n\nTime-based insertion\n: Define ad breaks at specific time points within programs. This allows you\n to insert ads at natural break points in your content.\n\nFor detailed information on creating programs with ad breaks, see Working with programs","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mediatailor/latest/ug/ssai-ca-integration.html"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Customizing ad break behavior with ad break suppression","context":"# Customizing ad break behavior with ad break suppression\n\nWhen you create a configuration in AWS Elemental MediaTailor, you can specify optional ad break\nconfiguration settings that govern the behavior of ad breaks, including the ability to\nconfigure ad break suppression. This allows you to tailor the ad break experiences for your\nvideo content to meet your specific requirements.\n\n###### Compatibility restrictions\n\nYou can't use ad break suppression with the following:\n\n* VOD and live-to-VOD workflows. Only live workflows are supported.\n* Server-guided ad insertion (SGAI) methods. Server-guided methods handle ad\n decisioning differently and don't require suppression configuration.\n\n###### Topics\n\n* Configuring ad break suppression","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mediatailor/latest/ug/ad-rules.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"MediaTailor Pricing","context":"## Channel Assembly Pricing\n\nA basic channel is limited to scheduling only video-on-demand (VOD) content and a standard channel can schedule both VOD and live sources.\n\n#### Cost per hour of a running channel","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/mediatailor/pricing/"}]}}

## Recent AWS announcements (What's New)

Newer than your training data may be. When these conflict with the documentation results above or with what you remember, prefer the most recent dated source.

{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports ad break discovery in Channel Assembly","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports ad break discovery in Channel Assembly. Previously, users had to create manual timing offsets for ad breaks in their channel schedule. However, with this new feature, when scheduling a VOD source as a Program for a channel, users can choose from detected ad break offsets in addition to scheduling at any segment boundary offset","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2023/10/aws-elemental-mediatailor-ad-break-discovery-channel-assembly/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports live sources in Channel Assembly","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports the use of live sources in Channel Assembly. This update allows users to schedule live content into linear channels created using Channel Assembly. Previously, users could only use transcoded and packaged HLS and DASH streams from VOD catalogs as sources. With this new feature, live streams from an origin such as AWS Elemental MediaPackage can also be used. There are two types of channel configurations: basic and standard","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/aws-elemental-mediatailor-live-channel-assembly/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports cue ad tags in Channel Assembly","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor has introduced support for cue ad tags in Channel Assembly when generating HLS outputs. This new feature allows users to configure ad breaks using cue ad tags instead of date ranges. With cue ad tags, Channel Assembly will add EXT-X-CUE-IN/OUT/CONT markers to the specific HLS outputs. Additionally, users can include asset metadata key/value pairs in the EXT-X-ASSET tag to signal additional content characteristics on a per break basis","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2023/07/aws-elemental-mediatailor-cue-ad-tags-channel-assembly/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now offers Yield Optimization to automatically fill ad breaks with Amazon Ads demand - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor has introduced a new feature called Yield Optimization, which automatically monetizes unused ad inventory during server-side ad insertion (SSAI) for livestreams. This capability is exclusive to publishers in the Amazon Publisher Services (APS) Streaming TV program and comes at no additional cost. Yield optimization turns unfilled ad breaks into monetized impressions, enabling publishers to maximize their revenue without requiring any extra infrastructure or client-side changes.\n\nThe feature is designed for large-scale live events, ensuring low latency and fast response times during peak viewership. Ads are stitched directly into the stream, ensuring seamless playback on every device. Publishers have control over which ads run in their streams by setting their own price floors and category rules.\n\nYield optimization is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available, including US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), Africa (Cape Town), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad, Malaysia, Melbourne, Mumbai, Osaka, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Paris, Stockholm), Middle East (UAE), and South America (São Paulo). Publishers can monitor ad fill rate improvements using MediaTailor metrics in Amazon CloudWatch and track revenue and earnings through the APS Publisher portal","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/mediatailor-yield-optimization/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports Low-Latency HLS ad insertion - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports low-latency HTTP Live Streaming (LL-HLS) ad insertion using HLS Interstitials. MediaTailor is a service for video providers to monetize live streams, linear channels, and video-on-demand content. LL-HLS reduces live latency by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges. MediaTailor uses HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, allowing for low-latency playback at scale and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This capability is ideal for live sports, news, betting and wagering, watch-party, and interactive live formats. Low-latency HLS ad insertion is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available. For more information, visit the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation. To get started, sign in to the MediaTailor console. MediaTailor supports LL-HLS by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges, using HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This results in low-latency playback at scale, making it suitable for live events and interactive formats where latency is crucial. The feature is currently available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is offered. For further details, interested parties can refer to the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation and sign in to the MediaTailor console to get started","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-elemental-mediatailor-low-latency-hls-ad-insertion/"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS MediaTailor Channel Assembly tier documentation"}

